// Undertaking Developments (D20), p.78-79.
(
    name: "Undertaking Development",
    die: D20,
    entries: [
        (1, 1, (title: "The Unlikely Ally", text: "The only person who knows the next step of your undertaking is a prisoner of a faction hostile to you. To succeed, you must infiltrate the enemy, and free someone who might be a monster, a madman, or your only hope.")),
        (2, 2, (title: "The Rival Party", text: "Another group of Unbroken, more ruthless and better equipped, is after the same objective. They see you not as peers, but as competition to be eliminated. You must now race against them, knowing they will exploit any weakness.")),
        (3, 3, (title: "The Truth is a Lie", text: "You discover a crucial piece of information that proves your initial hook was a deception. The \"sanctuary\" is a trap, the \"relic\" is a lure, the \"victim\" is the true monster. Your quest's purpose is now inverted, and you are the ones being hunted.")),
        (4, 4, (title: "The True Cost", text: "To proceed, you must do something terrible: betray a trusting community, sacrifice an innocent to distract a greater horror, or destroy a precious resource that others need to survive. Your success will be built on the suffering of others.")),
        (5, 5, (title: "The Third Player", text: "A new threat emerges, beholden to neither Choir nor Flesh. It could be a band of zealous witch-hunters who see all survivors as tainted, a coven of pagans performing their own apocalyptic rites, or a creature that slipped through the cracks in reality.")),
        (6, 6, (title: "Hostile Environment", text: "The environment itself becomes an active antagonist. A \"Flesh-quake\" reshapes the landscape, blocking your path with canyons of sinew. A \"Choir-storm\" of psychic glass shards forces you to take shelter. The world itself is trying to kill you.")),
        (7, 7, (title: "Humanity Remains", text: "You corner a target (a Penitent, an Apostate, a creature that defies definition) only to discover it retains a sliver of its former humanity. It pleads, weeps, or shows you a memento of its past life. Killing it now feels less like a necessity and more like an execution.")),
        (8, 8, (title: "The Ticking Clock", text: "An unforeseen event makes your undertaking time-sensitive. A Choir crusade is days away from your objective, a Flesh-blight is rapidly consuming the path forward, or a vital NPC is succumbing to mutation. You must hurry, or all is lost.")),
        (9, 9, (title: "The Enemy Within", text: "An NPC ally—or one of the players—begins to show signs of corruption. They hum the Choir's hymn in their sleep, or their skin takes on a waxy, flesh-like texture. Paranoia takes root: is it a sickness, or a betrayal?")),
        (10, 10, (title: "The Price of Power", text: "You find a powerful advantage: a pre-apocalypse relic humming with ancient truths, a ritual that silences the Choir's song, a source of clean water that could be the beginning of a new settlement. However, it is tainted. Using it will slowly corrupt you, physically or spiritually, forcing you to choose between your mission and your soul.")),
        (11, 11, (title: "The Burden of Hope", text: "A small group of desperate refugees (orphans, the elderly, the wounded) begin to follow you, seeing you as their saviors. Their needs are constant, they slow you down, and their presence makes you a much larger, more vulnerable target.")),
        (12, 12, (title: "The Haunting Past", text: "You encounter someone or something from a character's backstory, now horribly changed. A former lover is now a high-ranking Penitent, a childhood village has been absorbed by the Flesh, or a rival has become a cannibal chieftain. This forces a deeply personal confrontation.")),
        (13, 13, (title: "The Choice", text: "Your path is blocked by two warring horrors: a Choir legion on one side, a Flesh infestation on the other. The only way through is to help one defeat the other, knowing that whichever side you aid will grow stronger and more dangerous because of your actions. And probably turn on you immediately after.")),
        (14, 14, (title: "Complex Matters", text: "You witness something that shatters your understanding of the enemy. A Penitent disobeys the Choir's hymn. A piece of the Flesh displays intelligent, tactical behavior. The apocalypse is not as mindless as you believed, which makes it infinitely more terrifying.")),
        (15, 15, (title: "The Guardian", text: "Your objective is protected by a powerful, neutral entity. It could be an ancient pagan spirit, a pre-apocalypse saint, or a mad hermit who has lived there for decades. It is not inherently hostile, but it will defend its domain from all intruders, including you.")),
        (16, 16, (title: "A Glimpse of the Truth", text: "You find evidence that the Choir and the Flesh are not opposites, but are connected in some horrifying way. A Penitent's hymn contains notes that cause the Flesh to resonate and grow; an Apostate's dying gurgles form a perfect, angelic chord. The war is not a war at all.")),
        (17, 17, (title: "The Stolen Identity", text: "You learn that a key NPC—perhaps the one who gave you your undertaking—was killed and replaced by a creature of the new world. All your information is suspect, and you have been manipulated from the very beginning.")),
        (18, 18, (title: "The Poisoned Sanctuary", text: "You find a place that appears to be safe (fortified keep, a hidden valley, a cave system), but the sanctuary itself is the source of a slow, creeping horror.")),
        (19, 19, (title: "The Price", text: "You capture an enemy or find a tome that can answer your questions. The information it provides is vital, but the act of learning it exacts a toll: the character who learns it loses a precious memory, gains a new and terrible fear, or is now psychically marked for the enemy.")),
        (20, 20, (title: "True Goals", text: "You realize the object of your undertaking (the relic, the person, the location) is not the true prize. It is merely the key to a far greater, more dangerous objective that you were never meant to know about. Your simple mission has just become part of a much larger, more terrifying puzzle.")),
    ],
)
